ries":"Nightlife","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"gCmyE-atK7PLFsRDWa-iOA","review_id":"vaOCwx0MdCNJFIaRlY96Nw","date":"2016-01-15T22:52:56","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9417523145675659,"text_excerpt":"My husband and I went on Doctor Gumbo's combined food and drink tour. We attended several walking tours on our trip and Doctor Gumbo's was hands down the cream of the crop! I loved Dylan's presentation style. He's funny, informative, and makes history compelling and fun. He's a true storyteller, and in my opinion could have his own Food Network TV show sharing his passion for New Orleans food and history. We tried eight cocktails (shared between the two of us, four drinks each) and learned the fascinating history of the drinks. We also sampled several classic New Orleans dishes (gumbo, po boys, muffulettas, pralines, etc.) along with some fun surprises. This tour was a great way to try di..."},{"business_id":"gCmyE-atK7PLFsRDWa-iOA","review_id":"LfEqhPyAySqCHW7_Z0ORAQ","date":"2015-03-25T14:09:06","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9387290477752686,"text_excerpt":"Took my family on Dr. Gumbos Foodie Tour when they mentioned that they wanted to get a varied taste of NOLA. They were not disappointed and neither was I. We got more than we paid for ($55) and will be coming back when others are in town. The long and short of it: 1. Tour Guide. Dylan leads the tour from place to place and was nothing short of awesome. He offers tons of insight into NOLA history, food history and culture with plenty of wit and humor tied in. Made the tour all that much more enjoyable. 2. Restaurants. Dylan takes you to 7 places, but 2 are not really restaurant. It's 5 restaurants, a praline shop and a hot sauce bar (not Pepper Palace). 2 dishes at SoBou and 1 at the other..."},{"business_id":"gCmyE-atK7PLFsRDWa-iOA","review_id":"1Xyyu5I9oS9ooP1vpCL1mw","date":"2016-06-17T23:16:30","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9284325838088989,"text_excerpt":"The tasting/history tour with Tracy of Dr. Gumbo's tours was absolutely fantastic. She was a font of knowledge, was friendly, funny and had a lot of insider tips about New Orleans. She knew her New Orleans history like the back of her hand and you could tell she was a true native who loves her city. At each stop there was a new delicacy to try we ate about 9 different things and by the end of the tour we were all stuffed. Most stops were inside and had seating and air conditioning as well which was lovely. The nature of the tour was it everybody got to know each other and we got to meet a lot of new people who are all very friendly and pleasant. Overall a fabulous tour that I can't recomm..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"gCmyE-atK7PLFsRDWa-iOA","photo_id":"-cXxcnfvDUxEbXwRdngr6w","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/-cXxcnfvDUxEbXwRdngr6w.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8702497482299805},{"business_id":"gCmyE-atK7PLFsRDWa-iOA","photo_id":"6yYW-qB7x1sbvxa2BCCiCQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/6yYW-qB7x1sbvxa2BCCiCQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8596259355545044},{"business_id":"gCmyE-atK7PLFsRDWa-iOA","photo_id":"Ctw0tBZpvLzljxXJlgwC1g","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/Ctw0tBZpvLzljxXJlgwC1g.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7365165948867798},{"business_id":"gCmyE-atK7PLFsRDWa-iOA","photo_id":"MApl18Ii72PwUCSB3swFhA","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/MApl18Ii72PwUCSB3swFhA.jpg"